    <!-- Pro Tips Section -->
    <section class="guide-section guide-section-alt" id="tips">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="guide-section-header" data-aos="fade-up">
                <h2 class="guide-section-title">Professional Design Tips</h2>
                <p class="guide-section-subtitle">Insider knowledge from our design team to help you avoid common mistakes and create spaces that truly work.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                    <div class="guide-tip-card">
                        <div class="guide-tip-number">01</div>
                        <h3>Start With a Focal Point</h3>
                        <p>Every room needs an anchor—whether it's a fireplace, artwork, or statement furniture piece. Build your design around this focal point.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
                    <div class="guide-tip-card">
                        <div class="guide-tip-number">02</div>
                        <h3>Consider Scale & Proportion</h3>
                        <p>Ensure furniture fits the room properly. Oversized pieces can overwhelm a space, while undersized items can make it feel empty.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="300">
                    <div class="guide-tip-card">
                        <div class="guide-tip-number">03</div>
                        <h3>Create Visual Flow</h3>
                        <p>Use repeating colors, materials, or patterns throughout your home to create cohesion from room to room.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="400">
                    <div class="guide-tip-card">
                        <div class="guide-tip-number">04</div>
                        <h3>Mix Textures</h3>
                        <p>Combine different materials—smooth, rough, soft, hard—to add depth and interest to your design.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="500">
                    <div class="guide-tip-card">
                        <div class="guide-tip-number">05</div>
                        <h3>Invest in Quality Basics</h3>
                        <p>Splurge on key pieces like sofas and beds, then save on accessories that can be easily updated over time.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-lg-4 col-md-6 mb-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="600">
                    <div class="guide-tip-card">
                        <div class="guide-tip-number">06</div>
                        <h3>Edit Ruthlessly</h3>
                        <p>Less is often more. Remove items that don't serve a purpose or bring you joy to create a more intentional space.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

